v0.4.0 is tagged and pushed, and the release workflow (run 41761864594) was still in progress when I checked, so the crates.io publish hasn't been confirmed yet. If it fails, gh run list --workflow release.yml -L 1 will show why.

```
$ git ls-remote --tags origin v0.4.0
7f9d6d553e1bc279bc9e9c772cb47192365a64f2	refs/tags/v0.4.0
```

Why a release now: v0.3.0 was 15 days ago. The shallow clone showed only 51 commits since then; after git fetch --deepen=600 it was really 566, about 250 of them actual features and fixes. Without deepening, the changelog would have missed most of the span.

Changelog: ## [0.4.0] - 2026-11-04 leads with the default changes, each checked against its commit and against providers.rs at v0.3.0 and now:
• MCP stdio servers and shell hooks now start with provider API keys unset (YOYO_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB=0 turns this off).
• With no --model, openrouter now runs anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5 (was claude-sonnet-4-6) and google runs gemini-3.8-flash (was gemini-2.5-flash).
• Unknown or malformed flags are now refused with exit 2 before anything is sent.

The fixes are grouped by area and include #1131 (task 1 landed). One claim from my first draft was wrong and I fixed it before committing: /run, /bg and /watch were never scrubbed, and only the model's bash tool has the opt-in. There's an empty ## [Unreleased] heading above the new section, and scripts/extract_changelog.sh v0.4.0 pulls the section out correctly.

Version: Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock are at 0.4.0. The only other "0.3.0" in the code is a test value in commands_update.rs:916, not a claim about the current version, so I left it.

